    pg_ch('1. Architecture, Types & DDL Mastery', 'PostgreSQL Architecture: MVCC, Tuple Versioning (xmin/xmax) & Write-Ahead Log', 'postgresql mvcc architecture, xmin xmax dead tuples, postgres wal shared buffers, readers never block writers',
        '**PostgreSQL** is the world\'s most advanced open-source object-relational database, built around **Multi-Version Concurrency Control (MVCC)** where **readers never block writers and writers never block readers**.',
        ['**How `UPDATE` Really Works in Postgres**: In PostgreSQL, an `UPDATE` does **NOT** overwrite bytes in place—it marks the old tuple\'s `xmax` transaction ID and appends a **brand-new tuple version** (`xmin`) on a heap page! Concurrent `SELECT` queries simply read the snapshot version visible at their start timestamp.', '**Write-Ahead Logging (WAL)**: Every change is sequentially flushed to WAL before commit returns, guaranteeing zero data loss even on power failure.', '**Why `AUTOVACUUM` Exists**: Because `UPDATE` and `DELETE` leave old "dead tuples" behind for older active snapshots, `AUTOVACUUM` reclaims dead space asynchronously.'],
        [['`SELECT VERSION();`', 'Inspects running PostgreSQL engine version', 'Default TCP port is **`5432`**.'], ['`xmin` / `xmax` hidden system columns', 'Transaction IDs that created / invalidated each row version', 'Query `SELECT ctid, xmin, xmax, * FROM ...` in `psql` to see MVCC live!'], ['`shared_buffers`', 'Postgres dedicated page cache (typically 25% of system RAM)', 'Works alongside Linux OS page cache.']],
        "SELECT VERSION() AS postgres_engine, CURRENT_DATABASE() AS active_db;",
