    pg_ch('2. Advanced SQL, CTEs, Window Functions & JSONB', 'JSON vs JSONB Internals, Containment Operators (@>) & GIN Indexing', 'postgresql jsonb vs json, jsonb operators @> ->>, gin index jsonb_path_ops',
        'PostgreSQL lets you combine strict relational ACID tables with NoSQL document flexibility in the **same database** via **`JSONB`**—parsed decomposed binary JSON supporting sub-millisecond **`GIN` (Generalized Inverted Index)** lookups!',
        ['**Always Use `JSONB` (Almost Never `JSON`)**: `JSON` stores raw unparsed whitespace text (slower reads, no `GIN` indexing!); `JSONB` parses once on write into binary decomposed keys/types, deduplicating keys and enabling fast `@>` containment indexes!', '**`->` vs `->>` Operator Difference**: `meta -> \'plan\'` returns a **quoted `JSONB`** value (`"pro"`), whereas `meta ->> \'plan\'` returns **unquoted SQL `TEXT`** (`pro`)!', '**`GIN` Index Operator Classes**: Default `jsonb_ops` indexes `?`, `?|`, `?&`, and `@>`; `jsonb_path_ops` indexes `@>` (`WHERE meta @> \'{"role":"admin"}\'`) using **60% less disk space** and faster lookups!'],
        [['`data -> \'user\' ->> \'email\'`', 'Navigates JSON object and extracts leaf as `TEXT`', 'Remember: `WHERE data->\'active\' = \'true\'` vs `data->>\'active\' = \'true\'`!'], ['`data @> \'{"tags": ["vip"]}\'::jsonb`', 'Containment check (GIN index accelerated!)', 'Far faster than `->>` string scans when backed by a `GIN` index!'], ['`CREATE INDEX ON events USING gin (payload jsonb_path_ops)`', 'Compact hash-path GIN index for `@>` queries', 'Ideal for multi-attribute e-commerce filter facets!']],
        "SELECT id, product_name, price\nFROM products\nWHERE price > 20\nORDER BY price DESC\nLIMIT 5;",
        ['**Frequent `JSONB` Update Warning**: Remember MVCC! Updating 1 tiny nested key inside a `500 KB` `JSONB` column via `jsonb_set()` rewrites the **entire `500 KB` row tuple**! Keep frequently mutated hot counters (`views_count`) in regular integer columns rather than inside large `JSONB` blobs.'],
        [['question' => 'What is the difference between Postgres operators -> and ->> on a JSONB column?', 'answer' => '-> returns JSON/JSONB; ->> extracts the value as plain SQL TEXT', 'options' => ['-> returns JSON/JSONB; ->> extracts the value as plain SQL TEXT', '->> mutates the row in place', '-> works only on arrays', '->> requires superuser role']], ['question' => 'Which GIN operator class creates a smaller, faster index specifically optimized for @> JSONB containment queries?', 'answer' => 'jsonb_path_ops', 'options' => ['jsonb_path_ops', 'btree_text_ops', 'hash_json_ops', 'brin_minmax_ops']], ['question' => 'Why shouldn\'t you increment a page-view counter 100 times/sec inside a 1MB JSONB column in Postgres?', 'answer' => 'MVCC rewrites the entire 1MB tuple version on every UPDATE, causing severe WAL and table bloat', 'options' => ['MVCC rewrites the entire 1MB tuple version on every UPDATE, causing severe WAL and table bloat', 'jsonb_set only accepts strings', 'JSONB max size is 1KB', 'GIN indexes delete rows']]],
        'Compare when to store structured columns (`user_id`, `status`, `created_at`) vs dynamic attribute bags (`metadata JSONB`).'
